---
layout: base.njk
permalink: "/r/"
title: Ratings
description: What the words under the covers mean, in order.
---
{#- The scale, printed. Every rung in order on one page, canon at the top,
    each with its one line — the only surface that shows the whole ladder at
    once, and the answer to "how many rungs are there and where does this
    sit". A five-point score with no scale printed anywhere was deleted from
    this site on 2026-09-04 for exactly that failure; this page is what keeps
    the replacement from repeating it.

    Reached from the shelf's sort control and from every rung's own page. No
    nav link: it's a key, not a section. -#}
<article class="tag ratings">
  <header class="tag-head">
    <h1>Ratings</h1>
    <p class="tag-desc">Two words under every cover: what happened, and what I thought. This is the second one, top to bottom.</p>
  </header>
  <ol class="ladder">
    {#- Canon is the first rung since 2026-10-22 (it was a tagview, printed
        here by a special case). It keeps its gold badge, and links to
        /canon/ — the ten's own page — not to /r/canon/. -#}
    {%- for rung in collections.ratingPages %}
    <li class="rung rung-{{ rung.slug }}">
      {% if rung.slug == "canon" %}<a class="badge badge-g b-canon" href="/canon/">canon</a>
      {% else %}<a class="rating r-{{ rung.slug }}" href="/r/{{ rung.slug }}/">{{ rung.title }}</a>{% endif %}
      {% if rung.description %}<p class="rung-desc">{{ rung.description }}</p>{% endif %}
      <p class="rung-count">{{ rung.members | length }} game{% if rung.members | length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</p>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
    <li class="rung rung-pending">
      <span class="rating r-pending">pending</span>
      <p class="rung-desc">No verdict yet. Not started, still going, or stopped for reasons that weren't the game.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="rung rung-partial">
      <span class="rating r-pending">liked*</span>
      <p class="rung-desc">An asterisk on any rung means a partial verdict: I liked (or loved, or didn't) what I saw, but I didn't play enough to speak to the whole game.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</article>
